    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] A markup is added onto the total cost incurred by the producer of a good or service in order to cover the costs of doing business and create a profit.\n[2] Markup is the ratio between the cost of a good or service and its selling price.\n[3] As is is a legal term used to disclaim some implied warranties for an item being sold.\n[4] Murabaḥah, murabaḥa or murâbaḥah (Arabic: مرابحة‎ ‎ , derived from \"ribh\" Arabic: ربح‎ ‎ , meaning profit) is a term of \"fiqh\" (Islamic jurisprudence) for a sales contract where the buyer and seller agree on the markup (profit) or \"cost-plus\" price for the item(s) being sold."
